### Page 1 of 2

```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:

Mayor Patrick Collins, and City Council
FROM:

TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager
DATE:

February 9, 2022
SUBJECT:
Consideration of Bid #E-11-22 for furnishing Eight (8) light poles (17th Street
Lighting), for the City of Cheyenne, Engineering Department
______________________________________________

One (1) bidder responded to this bid, and the bid tabulation is attached.  This is for the purchase
of Eight (8) light poles, for future installation on 17th Street between Carey Ave & Pioneer Ave.

The One (1) Bid was received from:
1. Cheyenne Winlectric Company. Cheyenne, Wyoming.
a. Submitted a fully compliant Bid.
A “No-Bid” was submitted by the following vendor:
1. Supreme Lighting Design, New York.
a. Submitted a NO BID.

The bid was reviewed by Tom Cobb (Engineering), and Sam Berta (Engineering).  Their
recommendation is to accept the lowest responsive bid from Cheyenne Winlectric Company, for
the purchase of Eight (8) light poles.  The total cost is $140,576.00.

Funding:
030-20-2042-42-43420
(Special Purpose Option Tax - 17th Street Corridor Projects - 2012 Ballot)

030-21-2111-40-43105

(Special Purpose Option Tax - Overage Projects - 2012 Ballot)

$140,576.00
```

